================================================================================
5. TWO-SCALE RESOLVENT INTEGRAL SPLITTING (N = 24)
================================================================================
Splitting the Laplace integral at the boundary-layer scale u_N = 1 / (kappa*N)^2:
    D_N(x) = (1/x) int_0^{u_N} e^{-u/x} H_N(u) du  +  (1/x) int_{u_N}^infty e^{-u/x} H_N(u) du
           = D_N^{BL}(x)  +  D_N^{bulk}(x)

Physical interpretation:
    The relevant dimensionless ratio is sigma = x / u_N = kappa^2 * N^2 * x:
    - sigma << 1: resolvent kernel samples predominantly the boundary layer
    - sigma ~  1: transition regime between boundary layer and bulk
    - sigma >> 1: resolvent kernel samples predominantly the continuum bulk

Using exact algebraic closed-form evaluation:
    Term m:  (1/x) int_0^{u_N} e^{-u/x} e^{-kappa^2 m^2 u} du = [1 - exp(-(1/x + kappa^2 m^2) u_N)] / [1 + kappa^2 m^2 x]

Boundary layer threshold for N = 24: u_24 = 0.000289318

